// AgentV3 — the full text of the Bhagavad Gita for the golden "Bhagavad Gita reader" template (admin 2026-09-30:
// "haan, poori Gita ke 700 shloka daal do").
//
// 🔒 WHERE EACH HALF COMES FROM, because a scripture app must be able to say so.
//   • SANSKRIT: the ancient public-domain text, taken from the gita/gita dataset (data/verse.json, released under
//     the Unlicense), fetched 2026-09-30. Cleaned deterministically: speaker lines split out, the verse number
//     marks removed, and the source's encoding slips repaired — an i-matra typed before the conjunct it follows
//     (कश्िचत् → कश्चित्), a long ṝ typed as ृ + nukta (पितृ़न् → पितॄन्), श्रृ → शृ. Three verses were found by
//     counting syllables per line and repaired by hand: 5.8 (शृण्वन्), 17.23 (the opening ॐ was missing) and 17.25
//     (the last word was cut to मोक्षकाङ्क्षि). tests/theWholeGitaIsHere.test.ts keeps those classes out.
//   • HINDI BHAVARTH: written for NavBharatAI, one plain sentence or two per verse. It is NOT copied from any
//     published translation — the same dataset also carries two modern Hindi translations, and those are the
//     translators' copyright whatever licence the dataset carries, so neither was used.
//   • NUMBERING: Gita Press. Arjuna's question that opens chapter 13 in some editions is kept as verse 13.0, so
//     700 verses are numbered as most Hindi readers know them, plus that one.
//
// Data only. The app reads it as eighteen JSON files (src/gita/01.json … 18.json), one per chapter, so a
// builder that opens one reads one chapter — never the whole book at once.

export interface GitaVerse {
  /** Verse number within the chapter (13.0 is Arjuna's opening question). */
  v: number;
  /** Who speaks, when the verse opens a speech. */
  sp?: string;
  /** Sanskrit, one half-verse per line. */
  sa: string;
  /** Plain Hindi bhavarth, written for this app. */
  hi: string;
}

